// grpc-gateway/runtime/query.go), which decodes enum-typed query params such as
// backup_location_enumerate_options.provider_types and .statuses, looks the enum
// up via github.com/golang/protobuf/proto.EnumValueMap instead - a separate
// registry that gogo's RegisterEnum never populates. When that lookup misses, the
// gateway falls back to parsing the query value as a plain int32 with
// strconv.ParseInt, which fails on values like "S3" with
// `strconv.ParseInt: parsing "S3": invalid syntax`.
//
// Mirror every enum registration from api.pb.go/common.pb.go into the
// golang/protobuf registry too, reusing the same generated _name/_value maps, so
// query-string enum filters resolve correctly.
